# Learn React (TypeScript) Playground

A **zero-config React playground** where you just create `.tsx` files and they auto-render.

## Quick Start

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000 — the app auto-discovers and lists all experiments.

## How It Works

Every `.tsx` file in `src/experiments/` is **auto-discovered** via Vite's `import.meta.glob`.
You never need to update routes, imports, or config. Just create a file.

### Creating a New Experiment

Create a file in `src/experiments/`:

```tsx
// src/experiments/11-MyExperiment.tsx

export const title = "My Experiment"
export const description = "What I'm learning here"

export default function MyExperiment() {
  return <h2>Hello from my experiment!</h2>
}
```

Save → it instantly appears in the sidebar via hot-reload! 🔥

### Convention

| Export | Type | Required | Purpose |
|--------|------|----------|---------|
| `default` | `React.ComponentType` | ✅ | The component to render |
| `title` | `string` | ❌ | Display name in sidebar |
| `description` | `string` | ❌ | Subtitle in sidebar |

Files are sorted alphabetically — prefix with numbers (`01-`, `02-`) to control order.

## Included Experiments

| # | Topic | What You'll Learn |
|---|-------|-------------------|
| 01 | Hello World | JSX, props, conditional rendering |
| 02 | State | `useState`, counters, objects |
| 03 | Effects | `useEffect`, cleanup, `useRef` |
| 04 | Events | Click, keyboard, TypeScript event types |
| 05 | Lists & Keys | Dynamic lists, add/remove, key prop |
| 06 | Forms | Controlled inputs, validation |
| 07 | Custom Hooks | `useLocalStorage`, `useDebounce`, `useToggle` |
| 08 | Context | `createContext`, Provider, theme toggle |
| 09 | Debugging | Console strategies, render debugging |
| 10 | Error Boundary | Catch crashes, fallback UI, recovery |

## Features

- 🔥 **Hot Reload** — edit a file, see changes instantly
- 🔍 **Auto-Discovery** — new files appear automatically
- 💥 **Error Boundary** — component crashes don't break the app
- 🌙 **Dark Theme** — polished UI out of the box
- 📝 **TypeScript** — type safety with helpful hints

## Tech Stack

- [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/) — fast dev server & build
- [React 18](https://react.dev/) — UI library
- [TypeScript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/) — type safety
